{
  "_comment": "Localization spec §9 — resolved-per-language expectations. THE RULE, and the only one an engine runs: strings[<language>][<stringId>] -> the keying artifact's own strings.en -> the raw stored value. No status, no hash, no source text, no other fallback; the tables are full and every §7 rule is already applied to their values. 'keyedIn' names the artifact whose strings.en is that id's source tier. The 'data-asset-localized' cases drive scalar/array/map reads through the accessor, including inherited overrides in localizationVersion 2. A 'reach' says how the id is ARRIVED at through a character record — follow it rather than rebuilding the id, because an inherited value's key names the DECLARING ANCESTOR, not the character being read. The 'unkeyed' cases are the mirror image: a .sfd slot that ships LITERAL and has no row of its own, even when the literal equals another live key — read manifest.localization.dataAssets before implementing them. The lookup runs on the AUTHORED template: any engine-side variable interpolation happens AFTER this resolution. ASCII by design: this package pins resolution, not text encoding. GENERATED by src/__tests__/runtime/character-contract-fixtures.test.ts (inputs: the real JSON export; expectations: the resolved localization.json that same export produced) — do not hand-edit; regenerate with REGEN_FIXTURES=1 and re-copy into the three plugin repos.",
